            "actionTime": "12:28:54",
            "sourceSystem": {
                "code": 2,
                "name": "House floor actions"
            },
            "text": "GENERAL DEBATE - The Committee of the Whole proceeded with one hour of general debate on H.R. 471.",
            "type": "Floor"
        },
        {
            "actionCode": "H32400",
            "actionDate": "2025-01-23",
            "actionTime": "12:28:07",
            "sourceSystem": {
                "code": 2,
                "name": "House floor actions"
            },
            "text": "The Speaker designated the Honorable Dale W. Strong to act as Chairman of the Committee.",
            "type": "Floor"
        },
        {
            "actionCode": "H32020",
            "actionDate": "2025-01-23",
            "actionTime": "12:28:06",
            "sourceSystem": {
                "code": 2,
                "name": "House floor actions"
            },
            "text": "House resolved itself into the Committee of the Whole House on the state of the Union pursuant to H. Res. 53 and Rule XVIII.",
            "type": "Floor"
        },
        {
            "actionCode": "H8D000",
            "actionDate": "2025-01-23",
            "actionTime": "12:27:35",
            "sourceSystem": {
                "code": 2,
                "name": "House floor actions"
            },
            "text": "Rule provides for consideration of H.R. 471 and S. 5. The resolution provides for consideration of H.R. 471 under a structured rule with one hour of general debate and one motion to recommit. Also, the resolution provides for consideration of S. 5 under a closed rule with one hour of general debate and one motion to commit.",
            "type": "Floor"
        },
        {
            "actionCode": "H30000",
            "actionDate": "2025-01-23",
            "actionTime": "12:27:30",
            "sourceSystem": {
                "code": 2,
                "name": "House floor actions"
            },
            "text": "Considered under the provisions of rule H. Res. 53. (consideration: CR H312-335)",
